<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada buys Canadian dollars - traders.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada buys Canadian dollars - traders.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada intervened and bought Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars on Friday as the currency traded around the C$1.3960 level, dealers said.</p>
<p>The intervention was through brokers and considered heavy as the currency weakened through key support to a new two-year low.</p>
<p>Following the intervention, the Canadian dollar was trading at C$1.3949 after opening at C$1.3933 and Thursday's close of C$1.3943. Traders expected further losses.</p>
<p>The Bank of Canada does not comment on intervention.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416-941-8100))</p>
</text>
